      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1hb50f0'
    '|b||Expected punishment: five hundred dollars. Less than the motor, so the motor goes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:i2ok44'
    '|a||Where does the theft stop paying?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1scnr8y'
    '|a||Wherever p times f reaches a thousand: one in two with two thousand,':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:teajpn'
    '|a||one in ten with ten thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:aimje1'
    '|a||Join every such point, and that''s the deterrence line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:od1am5'
    '|b||Every point on the line deters equally. But they don''t cost the same. Catching more thieves takes police;':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||a bigger fine costs almost nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1zir59'
    '|a||So Becker''s own logic says: catch few, punish hard. Slide up the line, toward the corner.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1li9g84'
    '|b||With a twist Becker spotted himself. If offenders like a gamble, the chance matters more than the size; if they dislike risk, the size matters more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1f79mcv'
    '|a||So the model can''t tell us which dial is stronger. Only evidence can.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xxrlw6'
    '|a||Want the math behind the deterrence line?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:18z66w8'
    '|a||In symbols: the theft is deterred when p times f is at least g.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So the line is f equals g over p: halve the chance, double the punishment.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:137w0lk'
    '|a||And ten percent more of either dial raises p times f by the same ten percent. Only attitudes to risk break the tie.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:104jb4d'
    '|a||So the data must decide. Start with the chance of being caught: more police.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Hard to test. Cities with more crime hire more police, so police and crime rise together.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1xshtig'
    '|a||In 1997 Steven Levitt found a way round it: mayors and governors hire extra police before elections, crime or no crime.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1uwuz3t'
    '|b||Then Justin McCrary found an error in the weighting. Corrected, the estimates were no longer statistically significant.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1b1emot'
    '|a||Later studies found other natural experiments. Chalfin and McCrary''s 2017 review sums them up: ten percent more police, about four percent less violent crime and two percent less property crime.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:rf6a73'
    '|b||Now the other dial. California''s three-strikes law: a third felony, after two serious ones, means twenty-five years to life.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1xgoxqt'
    '|a||Eric Helland and Alex Tabarrok found that offenders with two strikes were arrested seventeen to twenty percent less often.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:106ni14'
    '|b||Real, but for an enormous jump in sentence. Per ten percent longer, about six-tenths of a percent less crime.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:t0biz0'
    '|a||And the eighteenth birthday, where the expected sentence more than doubles? Drag the age-18 bar to your guess: how much less crime per 10% longer sentence?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:abluxd'
    '|b||Barely at all, as David Lee and Justin McCrary found: about half a percent less crime per ten percent longer sentence.':
